## 1. History of India and Indian National Movement

### 1.1 Ancient India

#### Indus Valley Civilization
*Sources: NCERTs, Standard Texts*

Key features:
- Timeline: c. 2600-1900 BCE (Mature Harappan)
- Geographical extent: From Sutkagendor (Balochistan) to Alamgirpur (UP), from Shortugai (Afghanistan) to Daimabad (Maharashtra)
- Major cities: Harappa, Mohenjo-daro, Dholavira, Lothal, Kalibangan, Rakhigarhi, Chanhudaro
- Urban planning: Grid system, covered drains, Great Bath, granaries
- Economy: Agriculture, trade with Mesopotamia, domestication of animals
- Religion: Pashupati seal, Mother Goddess worship, tree and animal worship
- Script: Undeciphered
- Decline: Multiple theories (climatic change, Aryan invasion theory debated, ecological factors)

#### Vedic Period
- Early Vedic (1500-1000 BCE): Rigvedic period
- Later Vedic (1000-600 BCE)

#### Mauryan Empire
- Chandragupta Maurya, Bindusara, Ashoka
- Administration, Arthashastra context, Dhamma

#### Post Mauryan Period
- Indo Greeks, Shakas, Parthians, Kushanas
- Sangam Age

#### Guptas and Post Guptas
- Golden Age, administration, economy, society

### 1.2 Medieval India
- Delhi Sultanate
- Vijayanagara and Bahmani
- Mughal Empire
- Bhakti and Sufi Movements
- Regional kingdoms

### 1.3 Modern India and Freedom Struggle
- Advent of Europeans
- British expansion and consolidation
- Economic impact of British rule
- Socio religious reforms
- 1857 Revolt
- Indian National Congress and freedom struggle phases
- Gandhian era
- Revolutionary movements
- Quit India and Partition


### 1.4 Indian Art and Culture

#### Architecture
- Indus Valley: Urban planning, Great Bath
- Buddhist: Stupas, Chaityas, Viharas (Sanchi, Bharhut, Amaravati)
- Hindu Temple Architecture: Nagara, Dravida, Vesara styles
- Jain Architecture
- Islamic Architecture: Indo Islamic style
- Colonial Architecture
