## 1. What CSAT actually is

| Item | Detail |
|---|---|
| Official name | **Paper II** of the Civil Services Preliminary Examination |
| Popular name | CSAT — Civil Services Aptitude Test |
| Introduced | **2011** (Prelims became two papers: Paper I GS + Paper II CSAT) |
| Marks | **200** |
| Questions | **80** (all objective, 4 options, single correct) |
| Marks per question | **2.5** |
| Duration | **2 hours (120 minutes)** |
| Negative marking | **1/3 of 2.5 = 0.83 marks** per wrong answer |
| Qualifying mark | **33% = 66 / 200** |
| Role in selection | **Qualifying only.** Marks are NOT added to the Prelims cut-off or to the final merit. Paper I decides your rank. |
| Language | Hindi + English (bilingual paper) |
| Level | **Class X** (officially stated) |

### 1.1 The single most important consequence

CSAT is a **gate, not a race**. You need 66. You do **not** need 180.
But it is a hard gate — around **lakhs of aspirants fail Paper II every year**,
and the failure is nearly always one of two things:

1. **Time mismanagement** — getting stuck in 3 arithmetic questions for 20 minutes.
2. **Arithmetic panic** — never having drilled tables/percentages, so a Class-X
   question eats 4 minutes.

Both are fixed by drilling, not by talent. That is the entire design of this book.

> **Target for a serious aspirant: 100–120 marks (40–48 correct), in 90 minutes,
> leaving 30 minutes as buffer.** Anyone scoring 66 exactly is gambling.

### 1.2 Recent trend (what the paper looks like now)

| Block | Typical question count | Nature |
|---|---|---|
| **Comprehension (RC)** | 25–30 | 3–4 passages; the largest single block |
| **Basic numeracy** | 15–22 | percentage, ratio, average, time-work, speed, P&L, SI/CI, number system |
| **Data interpretation** | 5–10 | tables, bar/line/pie charts, sometimes 2 questions per set |
| **Logical reasoning** | 10–15 | series, syllogism, arrangements, blood relations, direction, coding |
| **Analytical / puzzles** | 5–8 | seating, ranking, clocks, calendars, cubes & dice |
| **Decision making / interpersonal** | 0–5 | judgement questions; in years they appeared they carried **no negative marking** |
| **General mental ability** | 3–5 | odd-one-out, mirror/water images, venn, counting figures |
